## What it does

Durability here means four things:

- A slow provider never holds a database connection.
- A request never waits on a provider after its data commits.
- A tunable changes without a code edit.
- A gate stops only real harm.

rat-stack uses [Effect](/lore/effect-basics)'s own primitives for each one, in real seams. Agents load the [durability skill](/skills/durability) before they change one of these seams.

Each card below has five fields:

- **Problem:** what goes wrong.
- **Primitive:** the Effect answer.
- **Seam:** where rat-stack uses it.
- **Fence:** the test or lint rule that fails on the bug.
- **Incident:** where the lesson came from.

The incidents come from drovr on 2026-10-23.

### 1. Lease a connection for the query

- **Problem:** a connection held across a provider call starves the pool.
- **Primitive:** `RcRef` with `idleTimeToLive`, borrowed inside `Effect.scoped`.
- **Seam:** `packages/database/src/connection-lease.ts`, used by the Hyperdrive Postgres run log. Each request gets its own `RcRef`, because workerd pins sockets to a request.
- **Fence:** `packages/database/test/connection-lease.test.ts`, a model over queries, bursts, and provider waits.
- **Incident:** drovr car #2350. `mysql.acquire` p95 rose from 0.06 s to 2.3 s while PostShiba was slow.
- **Principle:** [lease-connections-per-query](https://github.com/joelhooks/rat-stack/blob/main/skills/durability/principles/lease-connections-per-query.md).

### 2. Answer at commit; dispatch off the request

- **Problem:** a request kept open across a provider call times out its caller.
- **Primitive:** `waitUntil` at the edge, with a backstop that replays the same [idempotency](/lore/http-responses-need-validation) key.
- **Seam:** `joinIntakeLayer` saves a ready contact with a pending-delivery marker. `JoinRequest.afterResponse` runs delivery through `waitUntil`. A five-minute sweep redrives indexed pending contacts with their submission ids.
- **Erase:** the contact is removed after its event tombstone lands. The sweep retries indexed pending erases.
- **Limit:** record and sweep-index writes are separate. A failed index write can strand delivery or erasure. An early erase can also prevent the request's ready commit. [`packages/core/spec/README.md`](https://github.com/joelhooks/rat-stack/blob/main/packages/core/spec/README.md#weaker-environments) records both gaps and the operator backstops.
- **Fence:** `packages/core/test/join-answer-at-commit.model.test.ts` and `packages/core/test/intake-sweep.model.test.ts`.
- **Incident:** drovr's ingress forward. Five `POST /events` answered 503 after their events committed.
- **Principle:** [answer-at-commit](https://github.com/joelhooks/rat-stack/blob/main/skills/durability/principles/answer-at-commit.md).

### 3. Set a provider timeout once

- **Problem:** timeout literals in several layers drift apart.
- **Primitive:** a `Context.Reference` with a default, read at [layer](/lore/layers-make-dependencies-explicit) build, then `Effect.timeoutOption`.
- **Seam:** `DrovrIntakeTimeout`. Browser and agent intake both read it. The Worker sets it from `DROVR_INTAKE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS`. `JoinDeliveryDeadline` gives every delivery one 25-second budget across its retries, under the 30-second `waitUntil` allowance.
- **Fence:** `packages/subscriber-delivery/test/intake-timeout.test.ts`.
- **Incident:** drovr #2339 changed a PostShiba timeout by deploy.
- **Principle:** [one-timeout-at-the-boundary](https://github.com/joelhooks/rat-stack/blob/main/skills/durability/principles/one-timeout-at-the-boundary.md).

### 4. Bound work in flight

- **Problem:** a serial loop lets provider latency set throughput. An unbounded fan-out floods the provider.
- **Primitive:** `Effect.forEach` with `concurrency`, or a `Semaphore`.
- **Seam:** the application listing in `apps/site/src/interest/applications.ts` reads 8 at a time, in id order. `intakeRedeliver` stops at the first outcome other than accepted and returns the rest.
- **Fence:** `apps/site/test/intake-applications-concurrency.test.ts`.
- **Principle:** [bound-in-flight-work-with-keys](https://github.com/joelhooks/rat-stack/blob/main/skills/durability/principles/bound-in-flight-work-with-keys.md).

### 5. Scope waiters to the request

- **Problem:** a module-level `Deferred` or `Semaphore` in a Worker isolate makes one caller wait on another caller's work.
- **Primitive:** a `Deferred`, `Cache`, `Ref`, `Semaphore`, `Queue`, `Latch`, `PubSub`, `PartitionedSemaphore`, or `TxSemaphore` created inside one request or runtime [scope](/lore/scopes-own-resources).
- **Fence:** `rat-stack-patterns/shared-waiters`, with a rejecting and an allowed fixture per constructor in `packages/core/test/patterns-rule.test.ts`.
- **Incident:** drovr cars #2344 and #2348.
- **Principle:** [scope-waiters-to-the-request](https://github.com/joelhooks/rat-stack/blob/main/skills/durability/principles/scope-waiters-to-the-request.md).

### 6. Climb a flag with a ledger

- **Problem:** changing one value by deploy costs a plan, a readback, and another deploy to undo it.
- **Primitive:** a `Context.Service` flags [port](/lore/hexagonal-architecture) with `Layer` adapters and a declared lifecycle [machine](/lore/lifecycles-are-machines).
- **Seam:** the [flags](/systems/flags) [cartridge](/lore/cartridges) separates the `declared → rollingOut → on → removed` lifecycle from scoped evidence rungs. `flip_feature_flag` changes a rung. The default operator adapter commits position, receipt and projection marker in one Durable Object transaction.
- **Fence:** `packages/flags/test/writes.model.test.ts` and `packages/flags/test/lifecycle.model.test.ts`.
- **Incident:** drovr shipped `postshiba-send-hold` dark behind three rungs.
- **Principle:** [climb-flags-with-a-ledger](https://github.com/joelhooks/rat-stack/blob/main/skills/durability/principles/climb-flags-with-a-ledger.md).

### 7. Fail open on liveness, closed on harm

- **Problem:** a gate that refuses on delay stops good work. A fallback in front of real harm lets the harm through.
- **Primitive:** `Schema.TaggedError` refusals, `Effect.catchTag`, and bounded retries.
- **Seam:** the deploy driver refuses an unapproved replacement or deletion with `PlanRejected`. It retries content-version mismatches until a deadline. Failed flag replica reads follow the declaration's `failurePolicy`: catalog default or typed refusal.
- **Fence:** `packages/deploy/test/plan.test.ts` and `packages/deploy/test/content-propagation.model.test.ts`.
- **Incident:** PostShiba's p50 rose from 0.3 s to 8 s. 46 of 47 timed-out first asks still arrived, and drovr did not resend.
- **Principle:** [fail-open-on-liveness](https://github.com/joelhooks/rat-stack/blob/main/skills/durability/principles/fail-open-on-liveness.md).

## The standard

- Every pattern has a seam in shipped code. Toy examples do not count.
- Every pattern has a fence. The fence fails on a planted copy of its incident's bug.
- A provider call never runs inside a held database lease.
- The join answer does not wait on delivery. Its uniform response is not proof that every storage write succeeded.
- Each provider has one timeout value. Config sets it at the [composition root](/lore/structure-effect-by-domain).
- Every fan-out names its bound.
- Effect stays at the pinned version. These patterns add no dependency.

The idle lease of 250 ms is a guess. drovr lists the same value with an expiry. Measure it before you depend on it.

## How to check

1. Run `pnpm --filter @rat-stack/database exec vitest run test/connection-lease.test.ts`.
2. Run `pnpm --filter @rat-stack/core exec vitest run test/join-answer-at-commit.model.test.ts`.
3. Run `pnpm --filter @rat-stack/subscriber-delivery exec vitest run test/intake-timeout.test.ts`.
4. Run `pnpm --filter @rat-stack/site exec vitest run test/intake-applications-concurrency.test.ts`.
5. Plant a bug and watch its fence fail:
   - Hold the lease for the whole request.
   - Run delivery before the answer.
   - Put `"20 seconds"` back in the agent intake.
   - Make the application read unbounded.
6. Run `pnpm turbo run check test build --concurrency=1` for the full gate.
